# Rust
/target
# Cargo.lock is committed: this workspace builds binaries (cli, desktop app),
# not a published library, so a checked-in lockfile is the correct practice.

# Borehole's own index/cache data (never commit indexed repo data)
.borehole/
*.borehole.db

# Tauri build output
src-tauri/target
src-tauri/gen

# Coverage
coverage/
*.profraw

# Materialized fixture repositories are generated (each is its own real
# git repo, which git can't nest as plain files without turning it into a
# broken gitlink — see fixtures/README.md). Only the generator script and
# fixtures/README.md are tracked; run `fixtures/build-fixtures.sh` to
# materialize them before running tests that depend on them. CI does this
# as a step before `cargo test`. Each fixture's own NOTES.md is written by
# the generator script and lives inside its (gitignored) inner repo.
fixtures/*/
